   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Annual Output Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output Indicator</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.1.Number of Eritrean Diaspora professionals recruited and deployed in government institutions
1.2.Number of capacity needs assessments developed in different government institutions
1.3 Number of trainings/twinning programmes conducted</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2018">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">None</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ten Eritrean Diaspora professionals deployed in different government institutions to provide support in technical, technological, managerial and administrative services, capacity needs assessment, research works, promotion of culture, transfer of skills through training/workshops and twinning programmes to enhance the national capacity of the country.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Deploying Diaspora professionals through UNDP support, research work on understanding Eritrea&#x2019;s Position in Contemporary Geopolitics: Opportunities and Challenges is completed and submitted for government review and feedback. Ministry of Foreign Affairs budget proposal for 2022 and Concept Note on recent developments developed and submitted. An international political and systems analysis and the preparation of &#x2018;&#x2019;Eritrea Country&#x2019;s Report&#x201d; prepared deploying volunteer Eritrean Diaspora professional is expected to support the Ministry of Foreign Affairs in improving its systems and diplomatic relationships with international organizations. Historical books, articles and documents translated from Italian into English to give lessons to the young generation from the past history of Eritrea. A website layout for the Eritrean Diaspora Professionals and a database developed. Support was also provided to update old system of web design, establishment of digital library, recovery of hard drives and database of some public firms, such as, Asmara Palace, Rora and the Ministry of Justice. Capacity for production of animation, Video clips and comics enhanced. Basic knowledge and skills have been transferred to young men and women. Eritrean technicians enhanced their skills about sound arrangement and to work as an audio engineer, acoustician and designer for different projects and programs held by PFDJ.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ten Eritrean Diaspora professionals deployed in different government institutions to provide support in technical, technological, managerial and administrative services, capacity needs assessment, research works, promotion of culture, transfer of skills through training/workshops and twinning programmes to enhance the national capacity of the country.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">In the first year of CF/CPD 2022-2026, through Engaging Eritrea volunteer Diaspora professionals in the National Capacity Development Programme, six volunteer professionals are contributing to their respective areas of expertise deploying in different ministries and organizations. The professionals supported in creating and enhancing Document Management System (DMS), Food &amp; Beverage Management System, testing and implementing Stock Inventory System, underage and temporary Eritrean ID for the National Confederation of Eritrean Workers (NCEW) and its stakeholders. Assessed current global, regional, and neighboring countries political events, foreign relation experiences; monitored and analyzed latest social, economic, and political developments; prepared briefing and concept notes on contemporary issues, speeches, etc. in support of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs. Completed the Audio-Visual Studio of the Ministry of Agriculture and is ready for use. The report on the completion of the Studio has been presented to the Minister and Chiefs of Staff and they are glad that any important information, success story, lessons learned, etc. would be easily produced within the internal capacity of the Ministry and the production of audio book requested by Hidri Book Publisher is also in progress. Enhanced technical capacity to produce Eritrean context-based animations, games, cartoons, poetry, movies, etc. for kids and adults. As per the request of National Union of Eritrean Women 15 young people (13 females and 2 males) have upgraded their skills on Sound Technology attending relevant courses twice a week for four months (June-September 2022). Conducted research on the history of Eritrea, anthropology, and social data, and translated documents from Italian to English to assist the young generation learn from the legacy of past history.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2020-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">10 Eritrean Diaspora professionals deployed in different government institutions to support in capacity needs assessment, research, promotion of culture, transfer of skills through workshops and twinning programmes to enhance the national capacity of the country.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">UNDP deployed five volunteer Eritrean Diaspora professionals supported in enhancing capacities of different institutions. The Ministry of Foreign Affairs was supported on international political analysis and preparation of &#x201c;Eritrea&#x2019;s Country Report&#x201d; which is expected to support the Ministry in exchanging and improving its diplomatic relations with international organizations including UN/UNDP. Finalized Standard Operation Process (SOP) for the National Union of Eritrean Youth and Students&#x2019; ICT department and completed final version of the ICT policy.  Translation of three documents (Chi E Dell Eritrea, Martini&#x2019;s Book and Enrico Mania&#x2019;s book) on Eritrean history, anthropology, scientific, and social data is on track. 
Upgraded the skills of 2 selected Eritrean technicians working under the Research and Documentation Center of the Peoples Front for Democracy and Justice (PFDJ) on audio recording and sound arrangement to enable them work as an audio arrangers for different projects and programs. The research and translation from Italian to English of three historical documents (Chi E Dell Eritrea, Martini&#x2019;s Book and Enrico Mania&#x2019;s book) on Eritrean history, anthropology, scientific, and social data is on track. Short animation clip on CoVID19 was made and successfully published on the national Eri-Tv and is expected to increase public awareness and prevention of the corona virus outbreak. UNDP covers only costs of air ticket and accommodation of the Diaspora professional volunteers.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
